+# Agent Note: Preserve the active user request across compaction
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-03-compaction-active-request-retention.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Repeated model-written checkpoints can lose the current research question and stopping constraints. A live three-source research run retained its twelve-call and 250-word instructions in the first summary, then lost both in subsequent summaries and continued fetching instead of answering. The event log still contained the original request, but the request sent to the model did not. Nonempty summarizer output alone does not establish that it preserves user intent.
+
+## Decision
+
+The [basic compaction transaction](../../../../packages/compaction/compaction-basic/README.md) preserves the open turn's latest admitted `source.kind: user` content blocks independently of the generated summary. Retention applies only when the selected range contains that input or a prior compaction checkpoint derived from it. Original provenance, not text tags supplied by a tool or plugin, identifies the request. The replacement cites the original event and is reconstructable from the durable log.
+
+The transaction captures request content and the count of actual `tool/call` events before awaiting the summarizer. The count covers all tools since that request, including failed attempts and calls retained outside the replaced span; it is not an enforcement policy. A later request outside the span remains later input. Closed turns remain compressible. The complete framed replacement must shrink under the existing meter, so oversized retained inputs fail without removing their original history.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Prompt-only repair.** The summarizer already asks for explicit instructions to be preserved. Repeating that demand does not prevent lossy recursive summaries from discarding the exact request.
+
+**Changing model routes or context sizes.** Those changes would alter the operator's configuration and would not establish request preservation. This repair changes neither those settings nor tool permissions.
+
+**Retaining all historical user inputs.** This prevents ordinary closed-turn history compaction and can leave no reducible context. The retained input is limited to the latest one in the current open turn; older intent remains part of the summary.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Every affected checkpoint spends additional tokens on the unchanged request and progress framing. It can refuse a compaction that previously succeeded by discarding that request. It does not verify summary facts, reject all summarizer refusals, enforce call limits, or guarantee that the model answers. No session format or public configuration changes are required.
+
+Package regressions cover recursive lossy summaries, replay, source provenance, call accounting, steering, unrelated spans, closed turns, and shrink failure. The keyless headless overflow snapshot runs the real Loader and built package with compressible background context and asserts that the exact request and count survive. Deterministic preservation evidence is separate from live research-answer acceptance.
